0:{"buildId":"7afh9cBoHBO9HIwX4Lcyt","data":[{"rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[["$","$L2",null,{"toc":[{"depth":2,"url":"#forge-pushes-it-is-never-scraped","title":"Forge pushes; it is never scraped"},{"depth":2,"url":"#the-configuration","title":"The configuration"},{"depth":2,"url":"#bring-up-the-pipeline","title":"Bring up the pipeline"},{"depth":2,"url":"#what-happens-if-you-skip-the-collector","title":"What happens if you skip the collector"},{"depth":2,"url":"#turn-on-cache-metrics","title":"Turn on cache metrics"},{"depth":2,"url":"#which-metrics-exist","title":"Which metrics exist"},{"depth":2,"url":"#queries-worth-having","title":"Queries worth having"},{"depth":2,"url":"#the-grafana-dashboard","title":"The Grafana dashboard"},{"depth":2,"url":"#troubleshooting","title":"Troubleshooting"},{"depth":2,"url":"#faq","title":"FAQ"},{"depth":2,"url":"#whats-next","title":"What's next"}],"children":[["$","$L3",null,{"children":"Observability"}],["$","$L4",null,{"children":"Forge pushes OTLP and nothing else. Wire it to a collector, get the series into Prometheus under the names the shipped rules expect, and know which environment variables actually do something."}],["$","$L5",null,{"children":["\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Who this is for:"}]," you are running Forge for other people and need to\nsee queue times, cache hit rates and worker behaviour on a dashboard.\n",["$","strong",null,{"children":"What you'll have at the end:"}]," a collector receiving OTLP from every\nForge process, Prometheus holding the series under the names the shipped\nrecording rules query, and a Grafana dashboard drawing them. ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"Time:"}]," 30\nminutes."]}],"\n",["$","div",null,{"data-prerequisites":true,"className":"my-6 rounded-xl border border-border bg-surface-elevated px-5 py-3","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"my-0 font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-brand","children":"Before you start"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-1 text-sm text-muted-foreground [&>p]:my-0","children":["$","p",null,{"children":"A running deployment you can set environment variables on."}]}]]}],"\n",["$","$L6",null,{"as":"h2","id":"forge-pushes-it-is-never-scraped","children":"Forge pushes; it is never scraped"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["The binary has no ",["$","code",null,{"children":"/metrics"}]," endpoint and no configuration that creates\none. Forge builds three OTLP exporters at startup (logs, traces and\nmetrics) and pushes to whatever endpoint the environment names. Every\nPrometheus-shaped thing in this pipeline happens downstream of the process."]}],"\n",["$","$L7",null,{"children":"flowchart LR\n  NL[\"forge<br/>CAS · scheduler · worker\"]\n  COL[\"OTel Collector<br/>otlp receiver :4317\"]\n  PEX[\"prometheus exporter<br/>:9090 · namespace: forge\"]\n  PROM[\"Prometheus<br/>published on :9091\"]\n  GRAF[\"Grafana :3000\"]\n\n  NL -->|\"OTLP/gRPC push<br/>every 60 s\"| COL\n  COL --> PEX\n  PEX -->|\"Prometheus scrapes\"| PROM\n  PROM --> GRAF"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["That ",["$","code",null,{"children":"namespace: forge"}]," on the collector's Prometheus exporter is\nload-bearing, and it is the single most misunderstood part of this pipeline.\nThe instruments Forge declares are named ",["$","code",null,{"children":"cache.operations"}],",\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"execution.queue.time"}]," and so on, with ",["$","strong",null,{"children":["no ",["$","code",null,{"children":"forge"}]," prefix anywhere in the\nbinary"]}],". The prefix is added by the collector. Bypass the collector and you\nlose it, along with every shipped recording rule and dashboard panel. See\n",["$","$L8",null,{"href":"#what-happens-if-you-skip-the-collector","children":"what happens if you skip the collector"}],"."]}],"\n",["$","div",null,{"className":"my-6 flex gap-3 rounded-xl border px-5 py-4 border-brand/40 bg-brand-soft/40 text-foreground","role":"note","children":["$L9","$La"]}],"\n","$Lb","\n","$Lc","\n","$Ld","\n","$Le","\n","$Lf","\n","$L10","\n","$L11","\n","$L12","\n","$L13","\n","$L14","\n","$L15","\n","$L16","\n","$L17","\n","$L18","\n","$L19","\n","$L1a","\n","$L1b","\n","$L1c","\n","$L1d","\n","$L1e","\n","$L1f","\n","$L20","\n","$L21","\n","$L22","\n","$L23","\n","$L24","\n","$L25","\n","$L26","\n","$L27","\n","$L28","\n","$L29","\n","$L2a","\n","$L2b","\n","$L2c","\n","$L2d","\n","$L2e","\n","$L2f","\n","$L30","\n","$L31","\n","$L32","\n","$L33","\n","$L34","\n","$L35","\n","$L36","\n","$L37","\n","$L38","\n","$L39","\n","$L3a","\n","$L3b","\n","$L3c","\n","$L3d","\n","$L3e","\n","$L3f","\n","$L40","\n","$L41","\n","$L42","\n","$L43","\n","$L44","\n","$L45","\n","$L46","\n","$L47","\n","$L48","\n","$L49","\n","$L4a","\n","$L4b","\n","$L4c","\n","$L4d","\n","$L4e","\n","$L4f","\n","$L50"]}],"$L51"]}],["$L52","$L53"],"$L54"]}],"isPartial":"$@55","staleTime":"$56","varyParams":null},{"rsc":"$L57","isPartial":"$@58","staleTime":"$56","varyParams":null},{"rsc":"$L59","isPartial":"$@5a","staleTime":"$56","varyParams":"$5b"}],"isUpgradeableISRFallback":false,"a":"$@5c","rootVaryParams":null,"needsRuntimeRequest":"$@5d"}
